# Charas — a soft black pinch of resin rubbed off a living plant.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw it; that is what this file is for.
#
# ## Why it is not a small hashish
#
# item/hashish is an oblique slab: vanilla's own `item/brick` silhouette, because a pressed lump of
# hash is that same object — something made in a mould. Charas is the opposite process and gets the
# opposite silhouette: **an irregular ball**, hand-rolled, never pressed, never squared off. The
# two must not read as the same item at two sizes, because they are not a ladder — they are two
# methods, and the mod's whole colour rule is that colour follows process and nothing else.
#
# Nearly black, with a warm brown only in the lit edge. That is what resin taken off a living plant
# and never dried actually looks like: it oxidises as it forms, which is also why charas is the one
# black hash and why it keeps the monoterpenes drying destroys.
#
# Items are high contrast — vanilla items span a median 164 luminance steps — so even a near-black
# item needs its full ramp, and the highlight sits in one cluster up-left rather than as a gradient
# across the sprite. A corner-to-corner fade explains only 9-16% of the brightness in real vanilla
# items; that is pancake shading and it is the classic tell.

@palette default
. = none
1 = 020201      the rim, and the shadow side
2 = 0E0A07
3 = 1A130D
4 = 2B2118      the body — the strain entry's own colour
5 = 3E2F21
6 = 55402B      the lit face, up-left
7 = 7A5C3C      sheen
8 = B08F63      the wet specular: three pixels, up-left, and nowhere else

@texture item/charas 16x16 type=item
